Apple's <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> Case uses adhesive to attach to the device, according to people who have <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/are-we-able-to-talk-ultra-fold-cases-yet.2488329/page-7?post=34873347#post-34873347">picked one up</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iphone-duo-case.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="899" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1063419" /><br/>
The case comes in two pieces and uses adhesive strips along the inside edges to attach securely to an &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;. An included insert instructs users to peel off the adhesive's protective film, put each half on the Duo, and then press down to make sure it's well-adhered.<br/>
<br/>
The &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj; Case is made from polycarbonate and comes in Sand and Navy Blue. It is designed to protect the back of the iPhone where the camera bump is located and the front around the outer display. It has a cutout for the front display, and no protection for the inside of the device when it's unfolded.<br/>
